<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Greifswald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1456">1456</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Greifswald University</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greifswald">Greifswald</a> is a university in the Baltic town of Greifswald in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded in 1456 with the support of Duke Wartislaw IX and the burgomaster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-rubenow">Heinrich Rubenow</a>. It became Lutheran during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. Under Swedish rule from 1648 to 1815 it was the oldest university of the Swedish realm and a link between German and Swedish learning.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-greifswald.jpg" alt="University of Greifswald" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernst-Moritz-Arndt-Universität Greifswald · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uni_Greifswald_-_Siegel.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
